@page "/sponsor"

<PageTitle>Support BasketElo</PageTitle>

<div class="sponsor-page be-story">
    <header class="be-story-hero be-reveal" style="--reveal-order: 0">
        <div class="be-story-hero-copy">
            <p class="be-story-kicker">Support independent basketball data</p>
            <h1 class="be-story-title">A partnership that respects the reader.</h1>
            <p class="be-story-lede">Sponsorship can keep BasketElo free while connecting a thoughtful brand with people who care about basketball, analysis, and the story behind the numbers.</p>
            <a class="sponsor-primary-link" href="https://x.com/sergitm12" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Start a conversation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="be-story-orbit" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="be-story-orbit-core">
                <span>Placement policy</span>
                <strong>1</strong>
                <small>calm, clearly labelled sponsor</small>
            </div>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="be-story-section be-reveal" style="--reveal-order: 1" aria-labelledby="why-sponsor-heading">
        <div class="be-story-meta"><span class="be-story-index">01</span><span>The promise</span></div>
        <div class="be-story-body">
            <h2 id="why-sponsor-heading" class="be-story-heading">One beautiful placement, made to belong.</h2>
            <div class="be-story-copy sponsor-copy-columns">
                <p>The goal is not to fill pages with banners. A sponsor should feel like a relevant recommendation for basketball, data, analysis, tools, training, media, or the people who follow the sport.</p>
                <p>The format is a single, clearly labelled placement with a calm visual treatment and a direct link. No pop-ups, autoplay, aggressive tracking, or cluttered ad walls.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="be-story-section be-reveal" style="--reveal-order: 2" aria-labelledby="fit-heading">
        <div class="be-story-meta"><span class="be-story-index">02</span><span>The fit</span></div>
        <div class="be-story-body">
            <h2 id="fit-heading" class="be-story-heading">Useful for the project. Relevant to the audience.</h2>
            <div class="sponsor-principles">
                <article><span>01</span><div><h3>Who it could suit</h3><p>Basketball products, data platforms, coaching tools, sports media, communities, equipment, and thoughtful technology brands.</p></div></article>
                <article><span>02</span><div><h3>What you get</h3><p>A visible association with an independent basketball project and a placement that respects the reader’s attention.</p></div></article>
                <article><span>03</span><div><h3>How it works</h3><p>We discuss fit, agree on a lightweight placement, and review it together. Packages can follow once the right connection is clear.</p></div></article>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sponsor-contact be-reveal" style="--reveal-order: 3" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
        <div><span>03</span><span>Start a conversation</span></div>
        <div>
            <h2 id="contact-heading">Have an idea for a good fit?</h2>
            <p>Send a message on X and mention BasketElo sponsorship. Numbers can come later; the first step is finding a useful connection.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="https://x.com/sergitm12" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Message @@sergitm12 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </section>
</div>
